      "type": "{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"FAQPage\", \"mainEntity\": [{\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What does the n8n integration do?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"It connects your forms to n8n via webhooks, so submission events — created, updated, or deleted — trigger automated workflows in your other apps.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"How do I connect n8n?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Create a workflow in n8n with Formester as the trigger and copy its webhook URL, then paste it into your form's Automate → Webhook with the matching event type.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Which events can trigger workflows?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Submission Created, Submission Updated, and Submission Deleted — choose the one your workflow needs.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What if the workflow stops running?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Check the workflow's run history in n8n and confirm the webhook is saved and published in Formester. Submissions always stay stored in Formester.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What is Formester?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Formester is an online form builder for creating forms, surveys, and quizzes with a drag-and-drop editor or AI. It connects with the tools your team already uses — Google Sheets, Slack, HubSpot, Zapier, and more — so your form data flows wherever you need it.\"}}]}"
